.TH JUKEBOX 1 2026-10-20 "commonjukebox 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jukebox \- opinionated way to manage a music library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jukebox
.I command
[\fIflags\fR] [\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B jukebox
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help " | " help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jukebox
lists, searches and tags music files in a music library.
Files are found by extension
.RI ( .flac ", " .ogg ", " .opus ,
case-insensitive) anywhere under the library directory.
.PP
The library directory is set once with
.BR "jukebox init" ,
or given to each command with
.BR \-\-library .
Flags may be written with one or two dashes and must come before the
command's arguments.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR init " [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-codec " \fIname\fR] \fIdir\fR"
Store
.I dir
(made absolute, with a leading
.B ~
expanded) as the library in the config file, and create the library's
settings file if it is missing.
Prints how many audio files were found and warns if there are none.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace a different library that is already set.
.TP
.BI \-\-codec " name"
Codec the library stores new tracks in:
.BR flac ", " opus " or " vorbis .
A new settings file defaults to
.BR flac ;
an existing one is only changed when this flag is given.
.RE
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-library " \fIpath\fR] [" \-\-artist " \fIX\fR] [" \-\-album " \fIX\fR] [" \-\-genre " \fIX\fR]"
Print every track in the library, sorted by album artist (or artist when it is missing), album, disc and track number, ignoring case,
as
.RI \(lq artist " \(em " album " \(em " track ". " title \(rq.
The filters match the whole tag, ignoring case, and may be combined.
.TP
.BR search " [" \-\-library " \fIpath\fR] \fItext\fR..."
Print the tracks whose artist, album or title contains
.I text
(the arguments joined by spaces), ignoring case.
Output is the same as for
.BR list .
.TP
.BI "tag show " path\fR...
Print the artist, album artist, album, title, disc, track, year and genre
of each audio file in the given files and directories; missing tags are left out.
Does not use the library.
.TP
.BR "tag set" " [" \-\-dry\-run "] [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-artist " \fIX\fR] [" \-\-album " \fIX\fR] [" \-\-title " \fIX\fR] [" \-\-genre " \fIX\fR] [" \-\-track " \fIN\fR] [" \-\-year " \fIN\fR] \fIpath\fR..."
Write tags to each audio file in the given files and directories.
Only the flags that are passed are changed; an empty value removes the tag.
The flags set the
.BR ARTIST ", " ALBUM ", " TITLE ", " GENRE ", " TRACKNUMBER " and " DATE
tags.
At least one tag flag is required.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the files that would be updated without writing anything.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow
.BR \-\-title " or " \-\-track
when the paths contain more than one file.
Without it, such a command is refused, since every file would get the same value.
.RE
.IP
Errors on individual files do not stop the others;
all errors are reported at the end and the exit status is 1.
Does not use the library.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-library " path"
Use
.I path
as the library instead of the one in the config file.
Accepted by
.B list
and
.BR search .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
After a command, show that command's flags.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/commonjukebox/config
User config file, by default
.IR ~/.config/commonjukebox/config .
Lines have the form
.IR "key " = " value" ;
blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
The only key is
.BR library ,
the path of the music library; a leading
.B ~
is expanded.
.TP
.I library/.jukebox/config
Library settings file, in the same format, kept inside the library so it
travels with it.
The only key is
.BR codec .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, such as an unknown command or flag.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the library once, storing new tracks as Opus:
.PP
.RS
.EX
jukebox init \-\-codec opus ~/Music
.EE
.RE
.PP
List one album and search the whole library:
.PP
.RS
.EX
jukebox list \-\-artist Radiohead \-\-album "OK Computer"
jukebox search paranoid
.EE
.RE
.PP
Tag a directory of files and check the result:
.PP
.RS
.EX
jukebox tag set \-\-artist Radiohead \-\-year 1997 ~/Downloads/okc
jukebox tag show ~/Downloads/okc
.EE
.RE
